 ## Background
-The method is a standard technique in voxel-based game development for optimizing renderable geometry. It is widely used in engines like Minecraft and its clones to reduce draw calls and vertex count by removing internal faces. The specific implementation details regarding texture atlases and per-vertex lighting are documented in [S1, unofficial], while the application to collision mesh generation is described in [S2, unofficial].
